DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     These functions are used to maintain numbers stored in radix-64 ASCII
     characters.  This is a notation by which 32-bit integers can be repre‐
     sented by up to six characters; each character represents a digit in
     radix-64 notation.  If the type long contains more than 32 bits, only the
     low-order 32 bits are used for these operations.

     The characters used to represent “digits” are ‘.’ for 0, ‘/’ for 1, ‘0’ -
     ‘9’ for 2 - 11, ‘A’ - ‘Z’ for 12 - 37, and ‘a’ - ‘z’ for 38 - 63.

     The aa6644ll() function takes a pointer to a radix-64 representation, in
     which the first digit is the least significant, and returns a correspond‐
     ing _l_o_n_g value.  If the string pointed to by _s contains more than six
     characters, aa6644ll() uses the first six.  If the first six characters of
     the string contain a null terminator, aa6644ll() uses only characters preced‐
     ing the null terminator.  The aa6644ll() function scans the character string
     from left to right with the least significant digit on the left, decoding
     each character as a 6-bit radix-64 number.  If the type long contains
     more than 32 bits, the resulting value is sign-extended.  The behavior of
     aa6644ll() is unspecified if _s is a null pointer or the string pointed to by
     _s was not generated by a previous call to ll6644aa().

     The ll6644aa() function takes a _l_o_n_g argument and returns a pointer to the
     corresponding radix-64 representation.  The behavior of ll6644aa() is unspec‐
     ified if value is negative.

     The value returned by ll6644aa() is a pointer into a static buffer.  Subse‐
     quent calls to ll6644aa() may overwrite the buffer.

     The ll6644aa__rr() function performs a conversion identical to that of ll6644aa()
     and stores the resulting representation in the memory area pointed to by
     _b_u_f_f_e_r, consuming at most _b_u_f_l_e_n characters including the terminating NUL
     character.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     On successful completion, aa6644ll() returns the _l_o_n_g value resulting from
     conversion of the input string.  If a string pointed to by _s is an empty
     string, aa6644ll() returns 0.

     The ll6644aa() function returns a pointer to the radix-64 representation.  If
     value is 0, ll6644aa() returns a pointer to an empty string.

